  "discoveries": [
    "initramfs ROOT may contain the original PARTUUID= specifier; the first rejection attempt failed before identity comparison. Validated UUID resolution fixed this; no metadata mutation occurred.",
    "orphan_present is cleared at clean unmount. An initial strict feature check rejected the unmounted root; only known mount-state flags are now exempted, not permanent safety features.",
    "quota-tools rejected the subtree bind mount /srv/hosting as a filesystem argument. A descriptor- and kernel-verified native-root target was added without a caller-controlled path.",
    "Initial remount/print-state showed quotas on, but hard limits were not enforced. Explicit quotaon proved the cause; kernel accounting/enforcement flags now gate resume and native mutations.",
    "Manual diagnostic fixes are not the success evidence: the final binary replay from the pre-conversion checkpoint passed without them."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "One Debian 13 Hyper-V vendor image, ordinary ext4 partition and matching GRUB/initramfs-tools boot chain only.",
    "No Ubuntu/Rocky native qualification, LVM/RAID/LUKS or provider-managed boot/kernel qualification.",
    "Sequential before/after measurement phases, short samples and host caches/state; no precise causal overhead or statistical-significance claim. No HTTP, PHP, WAF or database transaction benchmark.",
    "A stable fsync median here does not prove quotas are free; random-write median was lower after conversion.",
    "Synthetic mount-dependent consumer only; not the real NGINX/PHP/OCI/agent service graph or complete installer/browser setup.",
    "Production one-shot/retry journal, installation locking, initrd/kernel coordination, power-loss recovery, aggregate capacity/OS reserve and migration remain open.",
    "Boot mutation marker is in memory, not power-loss-safe durable state; emergency recovery path was not destructively qualified.",
    "Existing high-level capability reporting still needs accounting-versus-enforcement semantics; the new native execution/startup gates check actual kernel state.",
    "Individual binaries changed during debugging. Fresh final replay shares one binary hash; the broader experiment is not an immutable release qualification."
  ],
